stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  [*] --> Idle
  Idle --> Turn

  state "Active voice turn" as Turn {
    direction TB
    [*] --> Preparing
    Preparing --> Listening : device and local components ready
    Listening --> Decoding : release or capture cap / accepted input
    Decoding --> Answering : local transcript admitted
    Answering --> Speaking : current answer admitted at Normal priority
  }

  Listening --> Terminal : hold under 250 ms or rejected input
  Speaking --> Terminal : completed or announcer preempts
  Decoding --> Terminal : new valid press / supersede
  Answering --> Terminal : new valid press / supersede
  Speaking --> Terminal : new valid press / supersede
  Turn --> Terminal
  Terminal --> Idle : cleanup complete / no replacement
  Terminal --> Turn

  note right of Idle
    Turn entry requires local opt-in and valid held PTT.
    Entry starts a new generation.
    Microphone off by default.
    Repeat held press and unmatched release do no work.
  end note
  note right of Listening
    Minimum hold 250 ms; capture at most 15 s.
    Open timeout 2 s; PCM at most 480000 bytes.
    Release ends the capture stream.
  end note
  note right of Terminal
    Turn to Terminal: critical preemption, mic off, user cancel or failure.
    Terminal to Turn: valid superseding press, cleanup, then new generation.
    Fence late callbacks; release transient resources.
    No interrupted answer resumes.
    Critical cancellation never waits on Voice locks.
    PCM handoff and zeroization: DEC-VOICE-BUFFER.
    Status contains no audio, transcript or answer.
  end note

